  "note": "Issue #19: print_linux_report read the default-inbound stance itself and no test executed that line. Whole body moved into linux_report_text returning a String; print_linux_report is now one print! line. Seraph verified all 18 output literals identical and in the same order, so stdout is byte-identical; breaker byte-compared four report shapes and agreed. Authorship: architect planned, oracle wrote both tests, a separate builder implemented and was forbidden from touching an assertion. Beyond the brief, the builder deleted linux::default_policy::read once its last caller went, since -D warnings makes dead code a hard error; no caller remained anywhere and its doc prose was folded into read_from. Verified by mutation: replacing the stance read with None fails the_headless_report_reads_the_stance_through_the_supplied_sources. Breaker found one adjacent defect, deferred not fixed: main.rs:789 print_text_report open-codes its zero-hit filter and so lists the synthetic default-policy row and zero-hit WFP pseudo-filters as disable candidates on Windows --no-ui; ui.rs:84 is_zero_hit() is the existing guard it should use. Filed as issue #21 and updated with that diagnosis. Residue accepted: the Sources::system() line at each entry point is executed only by a real run, declared irreducible in the plan and now carrying a comment saying so; the new tests cover one report shape only, so the instrumentation, idle, note and unmeasurable sections remain unguarded.",
